content.content:
---
name: navigator
description: Turns a request plus ranked code-search candidates into a refined brief that names the files to change. Read-only. Invoked by routes that need to locate code; never by a natural-language request.
tools: Read, Grep, Glob
model: sonnet
---
You locate where a change belongs and rewrite the request as a brief for the next agent. You never edit anything.

Two input forms. A prompt that starts with `Record:` is the record form, described at the end; every other prompt is the locate form below.

Locate form input: a request (bare prompt or ticket) and a ranked candidate list from code search. The list is a hint: it can miss files and rank unrelated ones high.

1. The candidate list is a starting point, not the boundary: search beyond it.
2. Verify every file you list (Files and Reuse) by reading its range with Grep and Read of line ranges, not whole large files. Never list a file you only saw in the candidate list.
3. For each file to change, read one hop away: the files it imports and its tests. Look there for code that already does part of the job.
4. Reuse lines are `path:line — signature — what to reuse`, from the declaration you read. Reuse is not listed under Files.
5. If no code concerns the request, leave Files empty and say what you searched under Open questions. A closest match is not a file to change.

Final message only, in exactly these sections. Keep Request, Requirements, Reuse and Open questions under 1000 bytes together. Files has no limit: list every file the change touches, including each sibling variant, view, translation and test file, one `path:N-M` per line; add `— why` only where it is not obvious.

## Request
The request restated with real code names (types, functions, modules).
## Requirements
One bullet per concrete requirement.
## Files
`path:N-M`, one per line, `— why` only when not obvious. Files to change only, repository-relative, no files that stay untouched.
## Reuse (reference only)
`path:line — signature — what to reuse`.
## Open questions
What the code could not answer.

Example (generic):

## Request
Add a `currency` field to invoices: `Invoice` model, `InvoiceService.create`, the PDF export.
## Requirements
- Store the currency code; default to the account's currency.
## Files
- src/billing/invoice.model.ts:12-40 — add the field
- src/billing/invoice.service.ts:55-90 — validate and default it
- src/billing/pdf/invoice-pdf.ts:20-70 — print it, sibling of the amount rendering
- src/billing/invoice.service.test.ts:1-60 — cover the default
## Reuse (reference only)
- src/accounts/account.model.ts:8 — `currencyOf(account: Account): string` — the account's currency already exists
## Open questions
- Should existing invoices be backfilled?

Record form. Input: the request, the files the run verified (each with the note that owns it, or `new note modules/<name>.md`), the existing owning notes in full, their current keywords and the keyword rules. Write nothing, read only what a keyword needs. Answer with only a bundle: one `=== modules/<name>.md` line per note, then the whole module file with its `## Keywords` section merged. Every keyword line is `- <keyword> - <path>`, the path being the one file that keyword identifies; a line without a path is dropped. Keep the existing keywords, add the words a ticket or user would write for this code (screen, element and feature names, domain nouns the request used), remove keywords whose path is a deleted file, never duplicate one. Every other section stays verbatim; it is ignored anyway. Create a note, in the shape Purpose, Key files, Depends on, Gotchas, Keywords, only for a name given as `new note`, never any other name. No code fences, no prose before or after, no files you did not change.

Example (generic):

=== modules/cart.md
# Shopping cart operations
## Purpose
- Holds the items a shopper is buying.
## Key files
- src/cart/cart.ts - add and remove items - items: addToCart
## Depends on
- none
## Gotchas
import type { LedgerEntry } from '#types/modules/evidence';

/** The navigator subagent as Claude Code names it in `agent_type`; a plugin agent is namespaced, a local copy is not. */
export const NAVIGATOR_AGENT_TYPE = /^(?:ambicode:)?navigator$/;

/** Where the SubagentStop hook leaves the navigator's final message, in the task directory; `navigator.brief` records it. */
export const NAVIGATOR_BRIEF_FILE = 'navigator-brief.md';

/** Where it leaves the answer to the `Record:` form, which `context.record` reads. */
export const NAVIGATOR_RECORD_FILE = 'navigator-record.md';

/** The route's model steps that launch the navigator, each with the file its answer is saved to. */
export const NAVIGATOR_ANSWER_FILES: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = { navigate: NAVIGATOR_BRIEF_FILE, learn: NAVIGATOR_RECORD_FILE };

/** Paths listed under `## Files` of a brief; "none" and an empty section count 0. */
export function navigatorFiles(brief: string): number {
  const lines = brief.split('\n');
  const from = lines.findIndex((line) => /^##\s*Files\b/i.test(line));
  if (from < 0) return 0;
  const end = lines.findIndex((line, at) => at > from && /^##\s/.test(line));
  return lines.slice(from + 1, end < 0 ? undefined : end).filter((line) => /^\s*[-*]\s+`?[^\s`]/.test(line) && !/^\s*[-*]\s+`?(none|n\/a)\b/i.test(line)).length;
}

/** The navigator waits while one of its steps is delivered and not yet completed; the file its answer goes to, else null. */
export function navigatorAnswerFile(entries: readonly LedgerEntry[]): string | null {
  const last = entries.findLast((entry) => entry.kind === 'step' && Object.hasOwn(NAVIGATOR_ANSWER_FILES, String(entry['step'])));
  return last?.['status'] === 'delivered' ? NAVIGATOR_ANSWER_FILES[String(last['step'])]! : null;
}

/** A module note whose keywords matched the request, with its whole text; `path` is how the notes listing names it. */
export interface MatchedNote { path: string; text: string }

/** At most this many matched notes go in: an irrelevant note costs more than it helps, and a note may be 2500 tokens. */
const MAX_MATCHED_NOTES = 3;

export const matchedNotesSection = (matched: readonly MatchedNote[]): string =>
  matched.length === 0 ? '' : `Matched notes (their keywords match the request; start here):\n${matched.slice(0, MAX_MATCHED_NOTES).map((note) => `=== ${note.path}\n${note.text.trim()}`).join('\n\n')}`;

const titlesSection = (notes: readonly string[], matched: readonly MatchedNote[]): string => {
  const shown = new Set(matched.slice(0, MAX_MATCHED_NOTES).map((note) => note.path));
  const rest = notes.filter((note) => !shown.has(note.split('  ')[0]!));
  return rest.length === 0 ? '' : `Project notes (read the ones that match the request before searching):\n${rest.join('\n')}`;
};

/** The project notes, where plan runs found reusable code; empty when the project has none. Matched notes come first, whole, and are not listed twice. */
export const notesSection = (notes: readonly string[], matched: readonly MatchedNote[] = []): string => {
  const parts = [matchedNotesSection(matched), titlesSection(notes, matched)].filter((part) => part !== '');
  return parts.length === 0 ? '' : `\n\n${parts.join('\n\n')}`;
};

/** The agent's whole prompt: the request, the notes that matched it, the ranking (a hint), and the other project notes. */
export function navigatorInput(request: string, ranked: readonly string[], notes: readonly string[], matched: readonly MatchedNote[] = []): string {
  const first = matchedNotesSection(matched);
  const titles = titlesSection(notes, matched);
  return `Request:\n${request.trim()}\n\n${first === '' ? '' : `${first}\n\n`}Candidates (ranked by code search):\n${ranked.join('\n')}${titles === '' ? '' : `\n\n${titles}`}`;
}
import { openWorkspace } from '#modules/config/workspace';
import { SEARCH_LAYER_DEFAULTS } from '#types/defaults';
import type { ProjectConfig } from '#types/modules/config';
import { literalPathspec, type Git } from '#platform/git/git';
import { AmbicodeError } from '#util/errors';
import { matchesAnyGlob } from '#util/glob';
import { normalizeRelative, toProjectRelative } from '#util/paths';
import { isSearchable } from '#util/path-classes';
import { harvest } from './harvest.ts';
import { tooBroad } from './refs.ts';
import type { Runtime } from '#types/composition';
import { COMMON_NAMES, LAYER_NAMES, type Declaration, type LayerName, type MapCandidate, type MapSymbol } from '#types/modules/search';

export const MAP_LIMIT_BYTES = 6144;
/** Wider than this many files, a term describes the project (`src`, a company name), not a boundary; the floor keeps tiny projects out of the rule. */
const TOP_FILES = 8;
/** Harvested names take the second half of a full term list, so a full first pass still lets them in. */
const PASS2_NAMES = 6;
const SPANS = 3;
const SPAN_CANDIDATES = 20;
/** Hits closer than this many lines read as one span. */
const SPAN_GAP = 8;
/** Per-term scores only order one call's list; content is weakest because a word can sit in any comment. */
const SCORE = { directory: 5, filename: 8, content: 2, named: 10 };
/** git grep already spreads one search over the cores: four at a time was the fastest on the 29-grep bench (1.45 s against 2.26 s serial). */
const GREP_CONCURRENCY = 4;

interface MapLayer { name: LayerName; ms: number; hits: number }

export interface MapResult {
  mode: 'prompt' | 'context';
  layers: MapLayer[];
  layersSource: 'config' | 'default' | 'route';
  terms: { pass1: string[]; pass2: string[] };
  /** The part of the ranking the 6 KiB text kept. */
  candidates: MapCandidate[];
  symbols: Record<string, MapSymbol[]>;
  collisions: string[];
  limitations: string[];
  omitted: number;
  /** The first line is the layer list; the rest is compact JSON. At most 6,144 bytes. */
  text: string;
  bytes: number;
  /** The `map` ledger entry's fields. */
  entry: Record<string, unknown>;
}

/** Top-ranked paths the ledger keeps so a later policy stage can scope rules to where the work is likely to land. */
const STAGE_PATHS = 8;

export function resolveLayers(mode: 'prompt' | 'context'): { layers: string[]; source: 'default' } {
  return { layers: [...SEARCH_LAYER_DEFAULTS[mode]], source: 'default' };
}

export interface MapInput {
  project: ProjectConfig;
  mode: 'prompt' | 'context';
  layers: readonly string[];
  layersSource?: 'config' | 'default' | 'route';
  terms?: readonly string[];
