Make navigator runs land in the same tracking as the other suites. Pick the mechanism from step 1:
- Option A: the navigator runner writes records in the existing history format into `evals/history.jsonl`, with a suite name such as `navigator`, its case ids, arm (navigator or bare), scores (recall and precision as the case score, or whatever the existing records use for score), cost, duration, and model, plus the existing chain or aggregate output if other suites produce one.
- Option B: plugin-eval cases with a scaffold, as described above.

Prefer the one that reuses the existing code path; don't build a second history format. History records must contain only ids, numbers and repo-relative paths, never prompt or ticket text. Bench and truth paths come from env/args as now. A machine without the NDA assets must fail clearly with a single line, and must not break `npm run evals` or the tests.
- Add an npm script, e.g. `npm run evals:navigator`, beside the existing `evals` scripts.
- Update `evals/README.md` with a short section.

