Repo: /Users/KillBill/Documents/projects/mine/ai/ambicode, branch `navigator-agent`. Read CLAUDE.md first and follow it (change before add, extend existing seams, tests ship with code, comments only for unobvious behaviour and ≤3 lines). Make no git state changes and launch no Claude or paid sessions; this costs $0. The bench data is NDA: never write prompt or ticket text or file contents into the repo, only case ids, numbers and repo-relative paths.

## Problem from the user
Navigator eval results are not recorded under `evals/cases/…/results` (or wherever the eval results the app charts read live). So they don't show in the charts as a navigator test case compared with a baseline. Right now the runner `evals/navigator/{run.mjs,lib.mjs}` writes only to `evals/history.jsonl` and `history.md` via `trackedRows`/`track.mjs`, plus its raw rows at `../ambicode-evals-assets/bench/results-nav/history.jsonl` with per-run dirs.

## Step 1: find exactly what the charts read
Look at an existing suite case's on-disk results: `evals/cases/<case>/results/` or `evals/results/`, for example a recent plan-accept or review-clean run from 2026-10-17. Identify:
